[01:23:09] @Gemini: I confirm your prior F001/F002/F003 family around Helper-T v2 and SymPy variable extraction is high-value, but there is a further downstream defect you did not trace: `_reconciliation_gate()` can amplify those upstream misclassifications into persistent winner-take-all verdicts because it compares raw confidence scalars across heterogeneous synthesis regimes without domain provenance. I detail that below as a new finding.

@CC2: Your checkpoint/context findings are directionally right. I am not repeating them. I am adding a distinct persistence-layer inconsistency: `signal_complete()` reports active models from mutable live state rather than the persisted round horizon, so completion artifacts can misstate which models actually participated in the sealed run after failures/restarts.

@DeepSeek: Your concern about `run_immune_pipeline()` threadpool failure handling is valid, but there is a stricter CDSFL issue still open: several disk persistence writes are non-atomic and can leave internally inconsistent recovery state across `round_XX.json`, `checkpoint.json`, and `completion_signal.json`. I cover the concrete locations and replacement code below.

[
  {
    "FINDING_ID": "F001",
    "SEVERITY": 0.83,
    "FLAW_CLASS": 5,
    "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.71,
    "DESCRIPTION": "In `bench/immune_agents.py`, `_reconciliation_gate()` merges v1 and v2 final verdicts by choosing the higher raw confidence when they disagree, but those confidences are not on a common scale. Evidence: `helper_t_cell_synthesize()` computes confidence as capped vote ratios (`reject_weight / total`, `confirm_weight / total`, then min with max individual), while `helper_t_v2_shadow()` computes confidence from max per-domain signals after optional log-odds aggregation and asymmetric rejection scaling only for decision, not stored confidence. Example from code: v2 can reject because `best_reject * 0.7 > best_confirm`, yet it stores `best_reject` unchanged; reconciliation then compares stored `v2c` against `v1c` directly. This is a semantic type error: the gate treats incomparable confidence meanings as comparable magnitudes, so disagreements can be resolved arbitrarily and systematically favor one synthesis regime.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, function `_reconciliation_gate()`. Raw confidences from `helper_t_cell_synthesize()` and `helper_t_v2_shadow()` have different semantics but are compared directly in the disagreement branch.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        else:\n            # Disagreement: higher confidence wins\n            if v1c >= v2c:\n                reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n            else:\n                reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n>>>>\n====\n        else:\n            # Disagreement: require same verdict-family support semantics.\n            # Do not compare heterogeneous confidence scales directly.\n            # Fall back to UNCERTAIN unless one side strictly dominates by\n            # verdict and confidence margin.\n            if v1v == \"REJECTED\" and v2v == \"CONFIRMED\":\n                if v1c >= 0.85 and (v1c - v2c) >= 0.20:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n                elif v2c >= 0.85 and (v2c - v1c) >= 0.20:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n                else:\n                    reconciled[fid] = \"UNCERTAIN\"\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = max(v1c, v2c)\n            elif v1v == \"CONFIRMED\" and v2v == \"REJECTED\":\n                if v1c >= 0.85 and (v1c - v2c) >= 0.20:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n                elif v2c >= 0.85 and (v2c - v1c) >= 0.20:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n                else:\n                    reconciled[fid] = \"UNCERTAIN\"\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = max(v1c, v2c)\n            else:\n                if v1c >= v2c:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v1v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v1c\n                else:\n                    reconciled[fid] = v2v\n                    reconciled_conf[fid] = v2c\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This changes downstream behavior in `run_immune_pipeline()` Stage 3a.5 and therefore affects `final_verdicts`, `final_confidences`, `rejected_findings`, `rejection_rate`, and both Regulatory T checks. Specifically, more disagreeing findings will become `UNCERTAIN`, reducing removals; therefore `regulatory_t_cell_check()` and `regulatory_t_v2_shadow()` thresholds should be re-evaluated against the new verdict distribution. The shadow log line in `_reconciliation_gate()` remains valid but will now log transitions to `UNCERTAIN` more often. VERIFIED: TRUE",
