    "DESCRIPTION": "In `bench/insect_brain.py`, `signal_complete()` reports `active_models` from mutable live state, not the set of models that actually participated in the persisted run. Evidence: `handle_model_failure()` destructively removes labels from `self.state.active_models`; `initialise()` resets it; `load_checkpoint()` restores whatever checkpoint last stored. `signal_complete()` then emits `\"active_models\": self.state.active_models`. If one or more models failed late, or the run resumed from a checkpoint with stale active model state, the completion artifact omits historically participating models and misstates experiment membership. For an audit artifact, this is incorrect.",
    "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/insect_brain.py`, function `signal_complete()`. The completion record uses current mutable `active_models` instead of deriving participation from persisted round data.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        signal = {\n            \"status\": \"CONVERGED\" if self.state.converged else (\n                \"FAILED\" if self.state.failed else \"INCOMPLETE\"\n            ),\n            \"reason\": self.state.convergence_reason or self.state.failure_reason,\n            \"total_rounds\": total_rounds,\n            \"total_findings\": total_findings,\n            \"active_models\": self.state.active_models,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        }\n>>>>\n====\n        participating_models = sorted({\n            model_label\n            for rr in self.state.round_records\n            for model_label in rr.model_responses.keys()\n        } | {\n            f.model_id\n            for rnd in self.state.all_findings\n            for f in rnd\n        } | set(self.state.active_models))\n\n        signal = {\n            \"status\": \"CONVERGED\" if self.state.converged else (\n                \"FAILED\" if self.state.failed else \"INCOMPLETE\"\n            ),\n            \"reason\": self.state.convergence_reason or self.state.failure_reason,\n            \"total_rounds\": total_rounds,\n            \"total_findings\": total_findings,\n            \"active_models\": list(self.state.active_models),\n            \"participating_models\": participating_models,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        }\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: Any downstream consumer reading `completion_signal.json` must switch from `active_models` to `participating_models` when it needs full-run membership rather than terminal-state liveness. Because `load_checkpoint()` restores `model_responses={}` for round records, this fix still depends on findings history to recover some participants; if a model produced responses but no findings before failure, its presence may still be lost after checkpoint recovery. That exposes a further dependency on preserving model response metadata in checkpoints or reconstructing it from `round_XX.json`. VERIFIED: TRUE",
