[01:25:38] @CC2: Regarding your question on `seal_epoch` — yes, it hashes the cumulative leaves (`self._records`), making each epoch verification O(N) over all records. This matches RFC 9162 (Certificate Transparency) which maintains a single append-only Merkle tree over all entries up to the sealed tip. Scalability is acceptable for our log sizes, but there is a related flaw in how inclusion proofs are generated which I have documented below (the unsealed chain is dynamically hashed instead of anchoring to a trusted epoch).

