      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/insect_brain.py`, `load_checkpoint()`: enumerates `all_findings` instead of joining on persisted round indices, so sparse/non-canonical checkpoints misbind metadata.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n        # Replay findings into a fresh convergence detector with persisted durations\n        self.conv_detector = ConvergenceDetector(self.config)\n        for round_idx, findings in enumerate(self.state.all_findings):\n            rr = rr_by_idx.get(round_idx, {})\n            duration = float(rr.get(\"duration_s\", 0.0))\n            self.state.round_records.append(RoundRecord(\n                round_idx=round_idx,\n                timestamp=rr.get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n                model_responses={},  # Not stored in checkpoint — available in round_XX.json\n                findings=findings,\n                finding_count=len(findings),\n                metrics=rr.get(\"metrics\", {}),\n                failures=rr.get(\"failures\", {}),\n                duration_s=duration,\n            ))\n            self.conv_detector.add_round_findings(round_idx, findings, duration=duration)\n====\n        # Replay findings into a fresh convergence detector with persisted durations.\n        # Require canonical dense ordering: checkpoint all_findings[i] must correspond\n        # to round_records entry with round_idx == i.\n        self.conv_detector = ConvergenceDetector(self.config)\n        self.state.round_records = []\n        total_rounds = len(self.state.all_findings)\n        for expected_round_idx in range(total_rounds):\n            rr = rr_by_idx.get(expected_round_idx)\n            if rr is None:\n                logger.warning(\n                    \"Checkpoint missing round_records entry for round %d; aborting recovery\",\n                    expected_round_idx,\n                )\n                self.state = BrainState()\n                self.conv_detector = ConvergenceDetector(self.config)\n                return False\n\n            findings = self.state.all_findings[expected_round_idx]\n            duration = float(rr.get(\"duration_s\", 0.0))\n            self.state.round_records.append(RoundRecord(\n                round_idx=expected_round_idx,\n                timestamp=rr.get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n                model_responses={},  # Not stored in checkpoint — available in round_XX.json\n                findings=findings,\n                finding_count=len(findings),\n                metrics=dict(rr.get(\"metrics\", {})),\n                failures=dict(rr.get(\"failures\", {})),\n                duration_s=duration,\n            ))\n            self.conv_detector.add_round_findings(\n                expected_round_idx, findings, duration=duration\n            )\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This is a fail-closed recovery change. Callers of `load_checkpoint()` must now handle `False` for structurally inconsistent checkpoints rather than getting a partially corrupted in-memory state. That propagates to any orchestrator recovery path using `brain.load_checkpoint()`. Because `persist()` always appends records in dense order, healthy checkpoints continue to load unchanged. If sparse-round recovery is actually required, the checkpoint schema must be extended to store round indices alongside `all_findings`; the current schema is insufficient.",
