      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/insect_brain.py`, method `extract_directed_messages()`.\nFIX: canonicalise message content before dedupe and prefer one message per recipient+canonical content, with deterministic precedence for explicit types over bare `@tag` matches.\n\nReplace the extraction body.\n<<<<\n        messages: List[DirectedMessage] = []\n        seen: set[Tuple[str, str]] = set()  # (recipient, content_hash)\n        active = set(self.state.active_models)\n\n        for pat_idx, pattern in enumerate(self._DIRECTED_PATTERNS):\n            for match in pattern.finditer(response_text):\n                recipient_raw = match.group(1).strip()\n                content = match.group(2).strip()\n\n                # Strip leading separator punctuation that leaked into content\n                content = content.lstrip(\":—- \\t\")\n\n                if not content:\n                    continue\n\n                # Resolve recipient — case-insensitive match against active models\n                recipient = self._resolve_model_name(recipient_raw, active)\n                if recipient is None:\n                    continue\n\n                # Skip self-directed messages\n                if recipient == model_label:\n                    continue\n\n                # Dedup within this extraction\n                content_key = (recipient, content[:200])\n                if content_key in seen:\n                    continue\n                seen.add(content_key)\n\n                msg_type = self._PATTERN_TYPE_MAP.get(pat_idx, \"extension\")\n                messages.append(DirectedMessage(\n                    sender=model_label,\n                    recipient=recipient,\n                    content=content,\n                    round_idx=round_idx,\n                    message_type=msg_type,\n                ))\n>>>>\n====\n        messages: List[DirectedMessage] = []\n        active = set(self.state.active_models)\n        priority = {\"response\": 3, \"challenge\": 2, \"question\": 1, \"extension\": 0}\n        best_by_key: Dict[Tuple[str, str], DirectedMessage] = {}\n\n        for pat_idx, pattern in enumerate(self._DIRECTED_PATTERNS):\n            for match in pattern.finditer(response_text):\n                recipient_raw = match.group(1).strip()\n                content = match.group(2).strip().lstrip(\":—- \\t\")\n                if not content:\n                    continue\n\n                recipient = self._resolve_model_name(recipient_raw, active)\n                if recipient is None or recipient == model_label:\n                    continue\n\n                canonical_content = \" \".join(content.split())\n                dedupe_key = (recipient, canonical_content[:200])\n                msg_type = self._PATTERN_TYPE_MAP.get(pat_idx, \"extension\")\n                candidate = DirectedMessage(\n                    sender=model_label,\n                    recipient=recipient,\n                    content=content,\n                    round_idx=round_idx,\n                    message_type=msg_type,\n                )\n\n                existing = best_by_key.get(dedupe_key)\n                if existing is None or priority[msg_type] > priority.get(existing.message_type, -1):\n                    best_by_key[dedupe_key] = candidate\n\n        messages = list(best_by_key.values())\n>>>>",
