      "DESCRIPTION": "The directed-message relay leaks stale messages into future rounds because it filters on `self.state.current_round` instead of the requested `round_idx`. In `bench/insect_brain.py`, `_format_responses_with_directed()` computes `current_round = self.state.current_round` and includes messages with `m.round_idx >= current_round - 1`. Evidence: relay payload generation is parameterized by `round_idx`, but this function ignores that argument entirely. If the orchestrator calls `relay_directed(next_round)` before `persist()` updates `state.current_round`, the filter still uses the previous round number and may include two rounds of messages instead of one. That is a temporal correctness bug in the relay window.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/insect_brain.py`, `_format_responses_with_directed()`, directed-message filter uses mutable brain state rather than the target round.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\n    def _format_responses_with_directed(\n        self,\n        model_label: str,\n        round_idx: int,\n    ) -> Tuple[str, bool]:\n@@\n        current_round = self.state.current_round\n        directed_to_me = [\n            m for m in self.state.directed_messages\n            if m.recipient == model_label and m.round_idx >= current_round - 1\n        ]\n====\n    def _format_responses_with_directed(\n        self,\n        model_label: str,\n        round_idx: int,\n    ) -> Tuple[str, bool]:\n@@\n        directed_to_me = [\n            m for m in self.state.directed_messages\n            if m.recipient == model_label and m.round_idx >= round_idx - 1\n        ]\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This aligns directed-message inclusion with `relay_directed(round_idx)` semantics and removes hidden dependence on when `persist()` last ran. No signature changes are required. If message retention pruning is later added, it should prune against actual round indices, not list positions, for the same reason."
