      "FINDING_ID": "GPT5_R6_F005",
      "SEVERITY": 0.81,
      "FLAW_CLASS": 5,
      "ABSTRACTION_INDEX": 0.64,
      "DESCRIPTION": "The claimed path constraint for CT v2 search-manifest verification is ineffective for grep/glob steps and too weak for read steps. In `bench/immune_agents.py`, `_verify_search_manifest()` only checks `os.path.isfile(file_arg)` or basename membership for `Read`, and for `Grep` it merely compiles the regex pattern. Evidence: it never verifies that the searched file/path targets are within `source_paths`, despite the docstring saying searches 'could actually have been performed'. A manifest step like `{tool:'Read', args:'/etc/passwd'}` verifies if the file exists, and `{tool:'grep', args:'secret.*'}` verifies even with no source target at all. This inflates CT v2 confidence via `test_severity = man_verified` on unverifiable or out-of-scope searches.",
      "PROPOSED_FIX": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, `_verify_search_manifest()`, manifest verification does not constrain search targets to reviewed source paths.\n\nFIX:\n<<<<\ndef _verify_search_manifest(\n    manifest: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n) -> Tuple[int, int, List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Mechanically verify the CT v2 search manifest.\n\n    Checks that the agent's claimed searches could actually have been\n    performed (files exist, grep patterns are valid).\n\n    Returns:\n        (verified_count, total_count, issues)\n    \"\"\"\n    verified = 0\n    issues: List[str] = []\n    source_set = set(str(p) for p in source_paths)\n    source_basenames = {os.path.basename(str(p)): str(p) for p in source_paths}\n\n    for step in manifest:\n        tool = step.get(\"tool\", \"\")\n        args = step.get(\"args\", \"\")\n\n        if tool in (\"Read\", \"read\", \"cat\"):\n            # Check file exists\n            file_arg = args if isinstance(args, str) else str(args)\n            # Try exact, then basename\n            exists = (\n                os.path.isfile(file_arg)\n                or file_arg in source_set\n                or os.path.basename(file_arg) in source_basenames\n            )\n            if exists:\n                verified += 1\n            else:\n                issues.append(f\"File not found: {file_arg}\")\n\n        elif tool in (\"Grep\", \"grep\", \"rg\"):\n            # Check pattern is valid regex\n            pattern = args if isinstance(args, str) else str(args)\n            try:\n                re.compile(pattern)\n                verified += 1  # Pattern is at least syntactically valid\n            except re.error:\n                issues.append(f\"Invalid grep pattern: {pattern}\")\n\n        elif tool in (\"Glob\", \"glob\"):\n            verified += 1  # Glob patterns are hard to invalidate\n\n        else:\n            issues.append(f\"Unknown tool: {tool}\")\n\n    return verified, len(manifest), issues\n====\ndef _verify_search_manifest(\n    manifest: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n    source_paths: List[str],\n) -> Tuple[int, int, List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Mechanically verify the CT v2 search manifest.\n\n    Checks that the agent's claimed searches are scoped to the reviewed\n    source paths and are syntactically plausible.\n\n    Returns:\n        (verified_count, total_count, issues)\n    \"\"\"\n    verified = 0\n    issues: List[str] = []\n    allowed_paths = {os.path.realpath(str(p)) for p in source_paths}\n    allowed_dirs = {os.path.dirname(p) for p in allowed_paths}\n    source_basenames = {os.path.basename(p): p for p in allowed_paths}\n\n    def _resolve_scoped_path(raw: Any) -> Optional[str]:\n        candidate = str(raw or \"\")\n        if not candidate:\n            return None\n        real = os.path.realpath(candidate)\n        if real in allowed_paths:\n            return real\n        base = os.path.basename(candidate)\n        if base in source_basenames:\n            return source_basenames[base]\n        return None\n\n    for step in manifest:\n        tool = str(step.get(\"tool\", \"\")).strip()\n        args = step.get(\"args\", \"\")\n\n        if tool in (\"Read\", \"read\", \"cat\"):\n            resolved = _resolve_scoped_path(args)\n            if resolved and os.path.isfile(resolved):\n                verified += 1\n            else:\n                issues.append(f\"Read target outside reviewed sources: {args}\")\n\n        elif tool in (\"Grep\", \"grep\", \"rg\"):\n            if isinstance(args, dict):\n                pattern = str(args.get(\"pattern\", \"\"))\n                target = args.get(\"path\", \"\")\n            else:\n                pattern = str(args)\n                target = \"\"\n            try:\n                re.compile(pattern)\n            except re.error:\n                issues.append(f\"Invalid grep pattern: {pattern}\")\n                continue\n            if target:\n                resolved = _resolve_scoped_path(target)\n                if resolved or os.path.realpath(str(target)) in allowed_dirs:\n                    verified += 1\n                else:\n                    issues.append(f\"Grep target outside reviewed sources: {target}\")\n            else:\n                issues.append(\"Grep step missing target path\")\n\n        elif tool in (\"Glob\", \"glob\"):\n            pattern = str(args)\n            if any(os.path.realpath(d) in os.path.realpath(pattern) for d in allowed_dirs):\n                verified += 1\n            else:\n                issues.append(f\"Glob target outside reviewed sources: {pattern}\")\n\n        else:\n            issues.append(f\"Unknown tool: {tool}\")\n\n    return verified, len(manifest), issues\n>>>>\n\nFOLLOW: This deliberately tightens the accepted manifest schema. `cytotoxic_t_cell_v2_shadow()` currently reads `search_manifest` opaquely, so after this change manifests lacking target paths for grep/glob will no longer earn confidence credit and CT v2 scores will drop until the prompt/output schema are updated to require scoped targets. That reveals a second necessary change: `_CT_V2_FALSIFIER_PROMPT` should tell the model to emit structured grep/glob args including target path. Without that prompt/schema update, this fix will correctly fail many previously over-credited manifests."
